goals.objective:
Add a new EasyLlama `bonsai` mode that serves Ternary Bonsai 2 27B (PQ2_0, ~7.2 GB) on a pinned PrismML-Eng/llama.cpp `prism` build with the Qwen3-Embedding-0.6B and BGE reranker GPU-resident and simultaneously co-resident on the RTX 5090 (32,607 MiB), then repoint Hindsight and the dotfiles templates at that mode and prove the retain queue actually drains — replacing the measured ~0-1 completions per 30 min the current mutually-exclusive qwen swap groups produce with a measured, sustained drain rate.

Success is observable when:
(a) `./run.sh --mode bonsai build` and `warmup` succeed; the mode ships a pinned PrismML fork binary at `/app/bin/llama-server-bonsai`; `config/config.bonsai.yml` mirrors `config/config.bonsai.yml.example`; `modes.bonsai` exists in `config.json.example`; `scripts/validate-config-yaml.sh` and `scripts/validate-code.sh` (ruff + `python -m pytest`) pass with 0 failures;
(b) `scripts/test-public-endpoints.sh bonsai` passes on response shape, not just status: `GET /health`, `GET /v1/models` (advertises the bonsai chat id, qwen3-embeddings, qwen3-reranker), `POST /v1/chat/completions`, `/v1/completions`, `/v1/responses`, `/v1/embeddings` (1024-dim), `/v1/rerank` (results present);
(c) GPU co-residency is proven, not asserted: llama-swap `/running` snapshots and `nvidia-smi` samples show all three models resident and serving at the same time with each contributing nonzero VRAM, routing is non-exclusive (no mutual eviction, llama-swap still the sole lifecycle owner), a chat request at >=131072 context completes with no OOM or engine/startup-gate error, and measured decode throughput (tok/s) plus peak VRAM for the three-model steady state are recorded;
(d) Hindsight compatibility is verified against the real provider shape: bonsai-chat returns parseable native `tool_calls` (llama.cpp `--jinja`/`--reasoning-format`) for a Hindsight-shaped request and `POST /v1/responses` answers, with the before/after reflect/consolidation error counts recorded;
(e) Hindsight (live `~/.config/hindsight/server.env` AND the dotfiles template `root/home/user/.config/hindsight/server.env.tmpl`) points its LLM, embeddings (still the Qwen3-0.6B at 1024 dims) and reranker at the bonsai mode's model ids on `127.0.0.1:8080`; health is ready; and over a >=30-minute measured window the retain queue reports a completion rate materially above the 0-1/30 min baseline with a measurably declining `pending_operations`, 0 new embedding/rerank errors, and 0 retry storms — the measured before/after ops/min and pending delta are reported;
(f) the 565 failed operations are individually reviewed and each is either retried to success or deleted/quarantined through the Hindsight operations API under a recorded, reversible policy, and the decision on `HINDSIGHT_API_ENABLE_AUTO_CONSOLIDATION` / pending-consolidation (62,632) is recorded with evidence rather than flipped silently;
(g) dotfiles carry the change: `.github/context/PROJECT/network-services.md` records the bonsai co-residency design and the measured drain, `templates/manifest.json` is regenerated by the renderer (not hand-edited), the renderer and secrets guard pass, and both repos are committed, pushed, `git status` clean with HEAD == origin/main.

Boundaries — In scope: the easyllama repo at /mnt/LIBRARY/llamacpp (new `easyllama/servers/bonsai.py` + registration in `easyllama/servers/__init__.py`, `config/config.bonsai.yml[.example]`, `modes.bonsai` in `config.json`/`config.json.example`, new `docker/*bonsai*` builder and runtime stages, `tests/`, `README.md`, `API.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`), the pinned PrismML fork ref, the three-model GPU co-residency routing design, the Hindsight server env knobs needed to unblock the retain pipeline, the live local stack, and the dotfiles deployment source (`root/home/user/.config/hindsight/server.env.tmpl`, `root/home/user/.config/systemd/user/easyllama.service.tmpl`, `.github/context/PROJECT/network-services.md`, `templates/manifest.json`). Out of scope: changing the behaviour of the existing qwen/llamacpp/turboquant/lucebox/spiritbuun/glm5.3-flash modes (qwen mode must stay green and intact), deleting or downgrading the existing qwen3-chat model or its NVFP4 weights, embedding the Bonsai vision tower / mmproj multimodal path, upstream PrismML-eng/llama.cpp, llama-swap, vLLM and llama.cpp code, the Hindsight application's own source and schema, wholesale deletion of the backlog, and any git history rewrite.

Constraints — (1) Stock llama.cpp must not be used for the chat model: `PQ2_0` is rejected by a stock build and a plain `Q2_0` file loads silently and emits garbage; the PrismML fork ref must be pinned to an exact ref/SHA and recorded in `config.json.example`. (2) Model artifact is `prism-ml/Ternary-Bonsai-2-27B-gguf` / `Ternary-Bonsai-2-27B-PQ2_0.gguf`, resolved cache-first so a warm `warmup` performs no Hub traffic. (3) The chat context must stay >=131072 (parity with qwen3-chat's 128K) and `-c` must be passed explicitly — bare `-c 0` would try the 262K training context and exhaust the card. (4) VRAM budget is 32,607 MiB total: the three-model steady state must fit with documented headroom; per-model ports stay pinned (existing bands 9000/9100/9200/... and the two-port stride, with a fresh `startPort` band for bonsai) so adding the mode never shifts another mode's addresses. (5) llama-swap remains the only model-lifecycle owner: no publish flags, no keep-awake/warm service, no external `/run` holder; the three models must not be placed in mutually exclusive swap groups. (6) The Hindsight embedding identity stays Qwen3-Embedding-0.6B at 1024 dimensions so existing vectors, the vchord index and the knowledge pages stay compatible. (7) Backlog mutation is API-only (`/operations/{id}`, `/retry`, `/delete`) and gated on the recorded policy; no direct SQL deletes. (8) `templates/manifest.json` is regenerated by the dotfiles renderer, never edited by hand; no secrets are written to either repo; no `git push --force` and no history rewrite. (9) Do not over-subscribe the 32-core host that also runs Hindsight and the other services — record the thread/slot budget chosen for the new mode and for Hindsight.

Verification contract — In an implementer's order: (1) `scripts/validate-config-yaml.sh config/config.bonsai.yml` clean; (2) `scripts/rebuild-and-warmup.sh bonsai` completes (build + warm past every advertised model); (3) `scripts/validate-code.sh` and `python -m pytest` in /mnt/LIBRARY/llamacpp with 0 failures; (4) `scripts/test-public-endpoints.sh bonsai` passes shape assertions for all seven endpoints, including a final chat request after embeddings to catch corrupt output across any unload/reload; (5) capture and paste `llama-swap /running` snapshots plus `nvidia-smi --query-gpu=memory.used` samples showing all three models resident simultaneously with nonzero VRAM each, the executed command lines, a >=131072-token chat that returns content, and the measured tok/s; (6) capture the Hindsight before/after: `/v1/default/banks/shared/stats` (`pending_operations`, `failed_operations`, `operations_by_status`) and the ops/min completion rate across a >=30-minute window on the bonsai stack versus the recorded ~0-1/30 min baseline, plus per-op evidence of the retry/delete decisions on the 565 failed operations; (7) re-read this objective and confirm each of (a)-(g) is evidenced; (8) confirm `git status` clean and HEAD == origin/main in both `/mnt/LIBRARY/llamacpp` and `/mnt/PROJECTS/repos/dotfiles`, and that the live config matches its tracked example.
